<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21142] LQA: add DOM support</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21142</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;LQA don't support DOM. Appropriate code and test case should be added.  Dom support is partly added by &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65511/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65511/&lt;/a&gt; (not landed yet) qmt_pool_lookup. However, it has to be disabled until qmt_pool_recalc start handling MDT data slave indexes as well as OST ones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt; /*
 * Until MDT pools are not emplemented, all MDTs belong to
 * global pool, thus lookup lqes only in global pool for the
 * DOM case. LQAs are skipped for DOM as LQA recalculation
 * doesn't account DOM grants. qid should be always passed
 * once LQA recalculation supports DOM.
 */


#define qmt_pool_lookup_arr(env, qmt, type, idx, stype, qid) \
                qmt_pool_lookup(env, qmt, type, NULL, \
                qmt_dom(type, stype) ? QMT_POOL_IDX_GLB : idx, true, \
                qmt_dom(type, stype) ? NULL : qid, false)&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
